# packages — the whole toolset, one line per tool: <name> <method> [key=val ...]
#
# Every tool tracks the LATEST version. The METHOD says how it's installed AND how
# it stays current — pick whatever is most natural for that tool:
#
#   pkg     package manager: Homebrew on macOS / conda-forge via `pixi global` on
#           Linux (rootless). Latest via upgrade.        opt: conda=<name> (if the
#           conda-forge name differs from the brew name)
#   cask    GUI app: Homebrew cask on macOS / official build on Linux.
#           opt: github=<owner/repo> (Linux release source)
#   conda   conda-forge via pixi on BOTH platforms (things Homebrew lacks)
#   npm     npm global (latest).                          opt: pkg=<npm-name>
#   uv      uv tool install (Python CLIs, latest)
#   self    the tool's OWN installer; it self-updates (this is fine/wanted).
#           opt: url=<installer>
#   source  build from git main (= latest).  opt: url=<git>  build=<cargo|make>
#
# Add a tool = add a line. Change how it's managed = change its method.

# --- language runtimes ---
node              pkg     conda=nodejs
python            pkg
rust              pkg

# --- editors ---
# neovim: brew's bottled stable lags the config; build master (~= nightly) with
# --HEAD (brew installs cmake/gettext as build deps). Drop head=true for stable.
neovim            pkg     head=true
vim               pkg

